      "derived_from": [
        "1053"
      ],
      "problem_statement": "The Python kernel engine (wrp_kernel/engine.py) and the TypeScript MCP server (receipts.ts) define different WRP state machines. The Python side lacks HOLD, still references PROPOSED (which migration 015 removed in TypeScript), and has SPECIFICATION/APPROVED/QUEUED states that don't appear in TypeScript. This is a critical divergence that blocks consistent pipeline behavior. The goal is to reconcile to a single canonical adjacency matrix, using the TypeScript version (which already has HOLD and has been running in production) as the source of truth, and remove the duplicate matrices from db_adapter.py and engine.py so the kernel is the single authoritative source.",
      "desired_outcome": "Reconcile WRP Adjacency Matrix — Python vs TypeScript divergence",
      "produced_files": [
