        "1056"
      ],
      "problem_statement": "The Kiro assessment flagged tackle/agent_chat.py, tackle/executor.py, and tackle/harness_launcher.py as duplicates of conduit equivalents. However, exploration reveals the two packages have diverged architecturally — tackle uses Python files named differently (executor.py, harness_launcher.py) while conduit uses executor_cloud.py and executor_registry.py with different interfaces. This plan addresses the divergence risk by either (a) formally archiving tackle in favor of conduit with a bridge layer, or (b) extracting shared harness/executor logic into a common library both packages import.",
      "desired_outcome": "Reconcile tackle/ vs conduit — deprecate or deduplicate",
