    {
      "plan_number": "0136",
      "title": "MEEP skeleton + CLI entrypoint (P1-1)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Create the MEEP project skeleton under nexus/python/meep/ with zero external dependencies (stdlib + dataclasses-json). Includes CLI entrypoint at meep/cli.py that accepts a prompt string and invokes the pipeline. This is the foundation that all Phase 1 stations build on.",
      "files_count": 11,
      "acceptance_count": 6,
      "dependencies": [
        "[]"
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-20 04:37:43+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-03 13:44:47+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0137",
      "title": "IRL classifier + IR resolver (P1-2)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Build Station 1 (IRL classifier) and Station 2 (IR resolver) of the Phase 1 vertical slice. IRL classifier is a keyword-based heuristic that maps a prompt text to a probability distribution over frozen InteractionArchetypes. IR resolver applies argmax to select the deterministic archetype. Both are pure functions with no side effects.",
      "files_count": 4,
      "acceptance_count": 15,
      "dependencies": [
        "\"[\\\"P1-1\\\"]\""
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-20 04:37:47+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-03 13:44:47+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0138",
      "title": "Spec compiler + lowering pass (P1-3)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Build Station 3 (Spec Compiler) and Station 4 (Lowering Pass / Freeze Boundary) of the Phase 1 vertical slice. The Spec Compiler takes an IRSelection + original prompt and produces a WorkRequestGraph (a small DAG of work nodes). The Lowering Pass freezes this into an immutable ExecutionGraph by resolving handler references and computing the topological order. After lowering, the graph is hashable and modification is detectable.",
      "files_count": 4,
      "acceptance_count": 9,
      "dependencies": [
        "\"[\\\"P1-2\\\"]\""
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-20 04:37:56+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-03 13:44:47+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0139",
      "title": "Deterministic scheduler + CER writer (P1-4)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Build Station 5 of the Phase 1 vertical slice. The scheduler is a deterministic loop that walks a frozen ExecutionGraph in topological order, executes each node (simulated handler in v1), and emits CER events for each state transition (NODE_START, NODE_COMPLETE, NODE_FAIL, NODE_SKIP). The CER writer appends events to an append-only log with a hash chain (each event includes prev_event_hash). After append, events are never modified, deleted, or reordered.",
      "files_count": 5,
      "acceptance_count": 9,
      "dependencies": [
        "\"[\\\"P1-3\\\"]\""
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-20 04:37:59+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-07-03 13:44:47+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0140",
      "title": "Replay engine (P1-5)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Build Station 6 of the Phase 1 vertical slice. The replay engine is a pure-function reducer that walks a CER event log and reconstructs the execution state (node_states, completed/failed nodes, overall completeness). It must be deterministic: same event log → same ExecutionState every time. It must also support partial replay: replay_until(log, event_index) to reconstruct state at any point.",
      "files_count": 2,
      "acceptance_count": 12,
      "dependencies": [
        "\"[\\\"P1-4\\\"]\""
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-20 04:38:04+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-20 05:25:02+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0141",
      "title": "End-to-end integration test (P1-6)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Wire all 6 Phase 1 stations together into a single end-to-end path: prompt → IRL → IR → Spec Compiler → Lowering → Scheduler → CER Log → Replay. The existing CLI (P1-1) should invoke the full pipeline end-to-end. Create integration tests that prove determinism, append-only, freeze boundary, and hash chain continuity across all stations.",
      "files_count": 4,
      "acceptance_count": 7,
      "dependencies": [
        "\"[\\\"P1-2\\\"\"",
        "\"\\\"P1-3\\\"\"",
        "\"\\\"P1-4\\\"\"",
        "\"\\\"P1-5\\\"]\""
