    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0178",
      "title": "Nebula Multi-Agent Cognitive Fabric — Role-Based Parallel Reasoning",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Design the concurrent multi-agent reasoning fabric over frozen GraphState snapshots: snapshot→dispatch→parallel retrieval→proposals→aggregate→resolve→governance→execute. Each agent role (Builder, Architect, Inspector, Explorer) gets a retrieval bias tuned to their level (L1 for Builder, L2/L3 for Architect, QUESTIONED for Inspector, all-levels for Explorer). Agents receive authority weights by context (Inspector→Very High on invariants, Builder→High on execution). The aggregate step handles overlaps and divergences via governance layer arbitration.",
      "files_count": 1,
      "acceptance_count": 1,
      "dependencies": [
        "[]"
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-22 03:55:55+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-26 05:50:15+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0179",
      "title": "Nebula Self-Healing and Feedback Learning System",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Implement receipt-driven self-healing: execution receipts (SUCCESS, FAIL_TRANSIENT, FAIL_SEMANTIC, FAIL_INVARIANT, SKIPPED) trigger review state transitions (SUCCESS→REVIEWED, FAIL_SEMANTIC→QUESTIONED, repeated failure→OUTDATED). Stability scoring formula: success_rate - failure_rate - invariant_violation_rate + reuse_frequency. Semantic diff detection across four drift types (input, output, control-flow, invariant). Self-healing proposes changes; governance approves them — never mutates directly.",
      "files_count": 1,
      "acceptance_count": 1,
      "dependencies": [
        "[]"
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-22 03:55:56+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-26 05:50:15+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0180",
      "title": "Nebula Governance and Mutation Authority Model (L0-L4)",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "Implement the four-layer governance hierarchy: L0 Conduit execution (observe only), L1 Self-healing (proposes), L2 WRP Validation (accepts/rejects), L3 Governance (final arbiter), L4 Meta-Governance (evolves WRP boundaries). Define mutation types (ADD_EDGE, SPLIT_NODE, RECLASSIFY, UPDATE_LEVEL, ADD_INVARIANT) and conflict resolution priority (invariant-preserving > execution-failure-driven > consistency repairs > optimization). Governance operates through explicit receipts, not inline mutations.",
      "files_count": 1,
      "acceptance_count": 1,
      "dependencies": [
        "[]"
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-22 03:55:58+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-26 05:50:15+00",
      "_src": "db"
    },
    {
      "plan_number": "0181",
      "title": "Nebula Temporal Graph Versioning and Branching Model",
      "status": "draft",
      "goal": "Implement temporal versioning for the WRP GraphState: MAIN (canonical), EXPERIMENTAL (testing), REPAIR (healing), SIMULATION (hypothetical) branches. A branch is a named, immutable pointer to a sequence of LOSMIR snapshots — not a copy of state. KernelState(branch, t) = Reduce(genesis → snapshot[t]). Branch graph is a DAG. MAIN is append-only linear history. Enables safe what-if analysis, repair workflows, and parallel semantic evolution without affecting production graph state.",
      "files_count": 5,
      "acceptance_count": 24,
      "dependencies": [
        "\"[\\\"0164\\\"]\""
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "created_at": "2026-06-22 03:56:05+00",
      "updated_at": "2026-06-27 15:00:22+00",
      "_src": "db",
