      "title": "NBK (Nexus Bootstrap Kernel) — Minimal Implementable Spec",
      "status": "archived",
      "goal": "NBK (Nexus Bootstrap Kernel) — Minimal Implementable Spec — Create a deterministic, minimal executable kernel that interprets causal graphs to grow the whole system, reducing complex layers (CSG-IR, LS-IR, etc.) to derived behaviors. Core primitives: Node (pure transformation), Edge (causal constraint), Trace (execution record), Lease (execution permission), Address (unique identifier). Everything else is derived behavior.",
